/-!
# The literal canonical denominator is generated by kernel displacements

Factoring the original elementary span by the actual commutator of its
section kernel produces a central cover of the same natural binary actor.
An unchanged support involution retains fixed codimension at most one.
The natural central-cover theorem therefore removes the residual kernel.
-/

public section
open Subgroup Stellmacher Theory.GroupTheory Representation Representation.BinaryOffender
open scoped IsMulCommutative commutatorElement
namespace CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section01
open Section03 Section03.InitialSource ChapterA.Section05To06 ChapterD ChapterD.UniqueFactor
